== Implementation (2026-11-07) ==
Tokens. ink3 7D8A81 -> 646E67, the same hue darkened until it clears AA on the worse of the two surfaces: 4.60 on
paper, 5.04 on card (was 3.13 / 3.43). One token, not a second "ink3 for text": a split would be a trap for the next
edit. New controlEdge 848A80 (paper 3.08, card 3.37) and accentControlEdge 968398 (3.04 / 3.33), for a border that is
the only thing saying where an interactive control begins. rule, rule2 and accentRule keep their values with a
comment saying why: they separate rows, and WCAG 1.4.11 asks 3:1 of what identifies a component, not of every line.
Control edges moved to the new tokens: file_readiness (the file box, both the ordinary and the nothing-passes
border), view_toggle (the outer border and the divider between the two halves), summary_grid (the card), verdict_card
(the standalone card). Nothing decorative was touched.
Semantics. sample_files: the two buttons keep their short visible words and gain semanticsLabel "Try this sample:
<title>" and "Download the sample file: <title>", so the eight buttons no longer share two names.
New app/lib/widgets/message_text.dart: one named, read-only, live-region node around the SelectableText used for
status and error messages, replacing the subtree's semantics. Applied at all four sites A8's one finding generalises
to: error_panel (kind = the panel's heading, else "Error"), backend_status_banner ("Server status"), home_screen's
503 queue notice ("Server busy") and version_notice ("Version mismatch", liveRegion false because it stays on
screen). The trade is written in the file: excludeSemantics drops the inner textbox's selection semantics, which is
the right way round, because an unlabelled editable field that cannot be identified is worse than a named message
that cannot be selected by gesture, and pointer selection still works.
200% text scale. The three rows measured as overflowing are Row(mainAxisSize: min) holding a Text that cannot shrink;
each Text is now Flexible, the idiom view_toggle.dart already used for the same reason. results_screen: the patient
id, the icon+label meta row, the legend row.
Risk icon (the plan's I1, an improvement, not a WCAG failure). New top-level riskIcon(RiskLabel) in risk_style.dart
is now the one place the icon is decided, and RiskStyle.of uses it so the two cannot drift. Drawn beside the verdict
in the grid row and in the standalone card's panel, in the verdict's own ink. Toxic and Ineffective share
danger/dangerBg, so before this the two most serious verdicts differed only by the word.
scripts/scientific_hash_policy.json: app/lib/widgets/message_text.dart added to core_paths (105 -> 106), sorted, no
duplicates; every tracked app/lib and backend/app source is in it.
No backend file changed.

== Tests ==
app/test/accessibility_test.dart, 19 passed. It recomputes WCAG 2.2 from the tokens rather than trusting a number
typed into a test:
  AC1 the arithmetic first reproduces the twelve A8 figures for the tokens B12 does not change (14.34, 5.50, 6.03,
      8.28, 7.68, 5.82, 4.96, 5.63, 6.72, 1.36, 1.64, 1.96) to two decimals. If that drifts the two measurements are
      no longer comparable and nothing else in the file means much, so it is asserted first.
  AC1 every colour used as text clears 4.5 on paper and on card; every verdict ink clears 4.5 on its own tint, on
      card and on paper; both control-edge tokens clear 3.0 on both surfaces; ink3 as an icon and every verdict ink
      as an icon clear 3.0.
  AC1 a source check, because a colour-only check can never catch a new control drawn with a decorative hairline:
      the four control-boundary sites must mention a controlEdge token within five lines of the border they draw.
  AC2 with semantics on, every ButtonStyleButton's accessible name on the samples card is unique, and each sample's
      title appears in exactly two of them.
  AC3 MessageText.nameFor is pinned both ways; a pumped MessageText matches a named, read-only, live-region node;
      and none of the four message files contains SelectableText( any more.
  AC4 for every ordered pair of distinct RiskLabels the word differs and the icon differs; Toxic and Ineffective are
      asserted to share a colour, which is the reason the icon has to differ; and every fixture verdict's icon is
      found on the rendered results screen.
  AC5 at 360px and 1440px, at 1.0x, 1.5x and 2.0x, opening every card produces no RenderFlex overflow. The test
      fails on overflow; the scratch measurement that found the defect only printed it.
flutter analyze: No issues found. The first draft of the semantics test walked the tree through pipelineOwner and
hasFlag, both deprecated, which analyze reports and the gate would have failed; it reads each button's own node
instead.
Flutter suite: 496 passed (B11: 477; +19). Backend suite: 1218 passed, 6 skipped, 4 failed - the same four identity
tests the re-bind refreshes, exactly as at B11 before its re-bind. B12 adds no backend test and changes no backend
file.

